{"label": "55722e7365cc43558d7e", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [{"word": "them", "refers_to": "the public miners", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}, {"word": "their", "refers_to": "the public miners' (Bitcoin mining operations)", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}], "conditions": [], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "Many public Bitcoin miners are pivoting to AI, selling their Bitcoin or winding down mining operations to fund AI data center buildouts.", "certainty": "certain", "speaker_is": "host", "speaker_evidence": "And we're seeing, you know, different stories where... So talk to us a bit about this idea from your perspective."},
{"label": "876662b7dc4e961d47e1", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [{"word": "It", "refers_to": "what is getting hacked (answered inside: other intermediaries, not Bitcoin)", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}, {"word": "it", "refers_to": "the fact that hacks hit intermediaries rather than Bitcoin", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}], "conditions": [], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "Recent crypto hacks have hit intermediaries rather than Bitcoin itself, which highlights Bitcoin's secure and unique nature.", "certainty": "certain", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "Mm -hmm. I mean, the good news about Bitcoin is... (Patrick Witt answering the host's questions about the administration)"},
{"label": "c49cd35dfd86efb624e0", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [], "conditions": [], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "Bitcoin is not a set-and-forget asset; hodling (self-custody) is an active process.", "certainty": "certain", "speaker_is": "host", "speaker_evidence": "The number of people that I talk to that haven't taken Bitcoin off the exchange is honestly quite frightening. (followed by the host's own ad read: Use promo code BTC Sessions 10)"},
{"label": "5e38ec62aa36eae80132", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [{"word": "it", "refers_to": "Bitcoin", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}], "conditions": [{"text": "all it has to do is stay decentralized and secure", "inside": true}], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "Bitcoin is a new system of measure for the first free market, and it only needs to stay decentralized and secure for that to emerge.", "certainty": "certain", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "And why that's interesting for this conversation to your initial question is how could we superimpose those two thoughts on what's going on right now? (Jeff Booth answering Natalie Brunell's question)"},
{"label": "6353ef6c32236e89f0cc", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [], "conditions": [{"text": "even if you have Bitcoin as a standard", "inside": true}], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "Even under a Bitcoin standard, speculators would still issue liabilities denominated in Bitcoin, so somebody will always be issuing some kind of loan.", "certainty": "certain", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "I mean, what do you make of this idea that... (the debate format; the selected speaker continues the MMTer's argument: That is my basic point. I am all for democratizing the current laws)"},
{"label": "316f66f81603ea55899a", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [{"word": "it", "refers_to": "Bitcoin (the price of Bitcoin)", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}], "conditions": [{"text": "if the price of Bitcoin goes higher", "inside": true}], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "A higher Bitcoin price makes it better collateral enabling more dollar credit, and this flywheel could be sustainable because Bitcoin is perfectly scarce while the dollar is not, as more dollars are created by design.", "certainty": "likely", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "It could be treasury companies like strategy and strive where we issue digital credit... (Joe Burnett explaining his thesis, then the host: Interesting. And when would you say that could be?"},
{"label": "d1e31dd4b7ddb686a18d", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [{"word": "it", "refers_to": "using Bitcoin privately via e-cash / freedom tech", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}, {"word": "it", "refers_to": "the emergence of the new technology (in the internet analogy)", "inside": true, "changes_assertion": "no"}], "conditions": [], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "It is now possible to use Bitcoin completely privately, pegged one-to-one in e-cash with private money and communications, but most of the world doesn't know it already exists, just as the world didn't foresee the internet's rapid emergence.", "certainty": "certain", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "So. So some of the things is kind of come out of my mouth next will be completely that people won't believe it... (Jeff Booth answering Natalie Brunell's question about the transition)"},
{"label": "43e6d312e1a1e6a4e33c", "speaker_changes_inside": "no", "view": "own_sincere", "referents": [], "conditions": [{"text": "if you want to have confidence that any purchases of Bitcoin are going to be legal", "inside": true}], "retraction": "none", "time_ok": "yes", "proposition": "To have confidence that purchases of Bitcoin for the Strategic Reserve are legal, authorization from Congress would be needed.", "certainty": "certain", "speaker_is": "guest", "speaker_evidence": "I can tell you the president's interested in it... So anyway, it's a challenging question. I would say the stance of the administration... (Patrick Witt, the White House official, answering the host)"}
]}
